WEBVTT

1
00:00:29,321 --> 00:00:32,742
The Animal Game was created
in Rio de Janeiro in 1892

2
00:00:32,825 --> 00:00:35,578
and was soon declared illegal.

3
00:00:37,872 --> 00:00:42,042
Attempts to suppress it
only made it more widespread.

4
00:00:43,461 --> 00:00:47,506
After the Great Catastrophe,
social chaos took over.

5
00:00:49,300 --> 00:00:53,179
The city changed,
but the game adapted and persisted.

6
00:00:53,929 --> 00:00:56,432
Now as a race between humans,

7
00:00:56,515 --> 00:00:58,976
enslaving the population and
enriching the elite.

8
00:00:59,977 --> 00:01:02,563
One group resists this exploitation,

9
00:01:02,646 --> 00:01:05,065
controlling territory and expanding
the resistance.

10
00:01:05,191 --> 00:01:09,987
<i>Bull runs towards the stairs,</i>
<i>but if he stumbles, it's over.</i>

11
00:01:11,363 --> 00:01:14,575
<i>Horse chose</i>
<i>to follow the alleys and avenues.</i>

12
00:01:14,658 --> 00:01:18,329
<i>It's a bit farther</i>
<i>but we already know his stamina.</i>

13
00:01:19,997 --> 00:01:23,209
<i>Things are heating up</i>
<i>in this decisive heat.</i>

14
00:01:23,292 --> 00:01:27,671
RIO DE JANEIRO
45 YEARS AFTER THE GREAT CATASTROPHE

15
00:01:29,673 --> 00:01:33,385
<i>And here comes the Rooster,</i>
<i>flying along the tracks of Arcos da Lapa.</i>

16
00:01:33,469 --> 00:01:36,514
<i>He won the last two heats,</i>
<i>and wants to be this season's victor.</i>

17
00:01:36,597 --> 00:01:39,183
Come on, Rooster.
First right in 120 meters. Come on.

18
00:01:45,898 --> 00:01:48,359
Bull, cross the street and overtake Horse.

19
00:01:48,442 --> 00:01:52,279
<i>And here's the Bull with no wings,</i>
<i>charging after the Horse.</i>

20
00:01:52,363 --> 00:01:56,325
<i>After the hill, he's moved up a position,</i>
<i>leaving Horse behind.</i>

21
00:01:57,409 --> 00:01:59,787
<i>These animals are running for their lives.</i>

22
00:01:59,870 --> 00:02:01,622
<i>It's dramatic. It's grim.</i>

23
00:02:01,705 --> 00:02:02,706
<i>It's a hit.</i>

24
00:02:07,753 --> 00:02:10,464
<i>But Bull's looking to take the lead.</i>

25
00:02:10,548 --> 00:02:12,007
Take Goat out of the race.

26
00:02:14,552 --> 00:02:19,682
<i>Bull takes Goat out! What a crash.</i>

27
00:02:19,765 --> 00:02:21,600
{\an8}<i>Will Goat come back from that?</i>

28
00:02:25,229 --> 00:02:26,814
<i>Rooster and Bull are out front.</i>

29
00:02:26,897 --> 00:02:29,692
<i>Neck and neck for first place.</i>

30
00:02:29,775 --> 00:02:32,403
<i>It's a close run.</i>
<i>This final's still up in the air.</i>

31
00:02:43,789 --> 00:02:46,709
<i>And the squad crosses</i>
<i>the Dry Sea of Botafogo</i>

32
00:02:46,792 --> 00:02:50,129
<i>to loop around the Perimeter</i>
<i>and head into the final stretch.</i>

33
00:02:54,216 --> 00:02:56,760
-How's it going?
-Rooster just passed Bull.

34
00:02:56,844 --> 00:03:00,973
<i>He knows he's fast. He prefers</i>
<i>to run alone and avoid confrontation.</i>

35
00:03:01,056 --> 00:03:03,726
-Go, damn you!
-Go!

36
00:03:05,769 --> 00:03:08,439
<i>Whoever bet right,</i>
<i>hold on to that lucky ticket.</i>

37
00:03:08,522 --> 00:03:11,567
<i>If your animal wins,</i>
<i>food and booze are guaranteed.</i>

38
00:03:11,650 --> 00:03:13,736
<i>It helps your family and clears the debts.</i>

39
00:03:15,154 --> 00:03:16,363
<i>There's the Tigress.</i>

40
00:03:16,447 --> 00:03:19,825
<i>She's mad. She's after Horse meat.</i>

41
00:03:25,623 --> 00:03:27,750
<i>The animals are close</i>
<i>to the Perimeter wall.</i>

42
00:03:27,833 --> 00:03:31,295
<i>Now they will cover the 3 kilometers</i>
<i>to the finish line.</i>

43
00:03:31,378 --> 00:03:33,756
<i>No one's crazy enough</i>
<i>to want to take a shortcut.</i>

44
00:03:33,839 --> 00:03:35,299
<i>In there, they don't stand for it.</i>

45
00:03:35,382 --> 00:03:37,134
They are nearly here. Come on.

46
00:03:43,474 --> 00:03:46,977
<i>Any animal that goes in there is hunted,</i>
<i>pursued and massacred.</i>

47
00:03:47,061 --> 00:03:49,772
<i>It's the resistance. They hate us.</i>

48
00:03:52,024 --> 00:03:54,068
<i>Rooster reached the wall first.</i>

49
00:03:54,151 --> 00:03:55,945
Bull, can you see Rooster?

50
00:03:56,028 --> 00:03:57,112
<i>Close in.</i>

51
00:04:00,032 --> 00:04:03,243
<i>-He's the only thing in your way.</i>
<i>-Look who's here. It's Bull.</i>

52
00:04:03,327 --> 00:04:04,286
Take him out.

53
00:04:05,371 --> 00:04:06,705
<i>Use the wall.</i>

54
00:04:12,002 --> 00:04:16,215
<i>Bull makes shredded chicken. Amazing!</i>

55
00:04:16,298 --> 00:04:19,218
<i>Bull takes first place again.</i>

56
00:04:21,303 --> 00:04:25,015
{\an8}<i>Rooster got run over</i>
<i>and is now in last place.</i>

57
00:04:25,099 --> 00:04:26,934
{\an8}<i>Things are going badly for him.</i>

58
00:04:27,977 --> 00:04:30,145
<i>Everyone's overtaken you. You are last.</i>

59
00:04:30,229 --> 00:04:32,231
<i>Help me. I need to win.</i>

60
00:04:32,314 --> 00:04:34,483
-Go into the Perimeter.
-<i>The Perimeter?</i>

61
00:04:36,360 --> 00:04:37,653
It's the only way.

62
00:04:37,736 --> 00:04:40,322
<i>The animals are all turning the corner.</i>

63
00:04:40,406 --> 00:04:44,910
<i>If you cut through the Perimeter,</i>
<i>you can still win.</i>

64
00:04:44,994 --> 00:04:45,869
Okay.

65
00:04:47,496 --> 00:04:49,540
<i>What's Rooster going to do?</i>

66
00:04:49,623 --> 00:04:52,626
Not the Perimeter, damn it!

67
00:04:55,004 --> 00:04:56,922
It's no use. He's in there, it's over.

68
00:04:57,006 --> 00:05:00,134
<i>He's in the Perimeter of Death.</i>
<i>The game doesn't fly in there.</i>

69
00:05:00,759 --> 00:05:02,511
<i>Animals are unlucky in there.</i>

70
00:05:03,137 --> 00:05:05,305
I'm in, damn it. Now help me.

71
00:05:05,389 --> 00:05:07,266
<i>That Rooster is screwed.</i>

72
00:05:07,349 --> 00:05:09,518
<i>Any animal that goes in there gets hunted.</i>

73
00:05:09,601 --> 00:05:14,064
{\an8}<i>Face the Hunter and you'll see.</i>
<i>He can take on any animal.</i>

74
00:05:28,328 --> 00:05:29,538
Who's his collateral?

75
00:05:30,789 --> 00:05:33,751
-This guy.
-He's already lost.

76
00:05:33,834 --> 00:05:35,711
<i>Rooster's collateral is his nephew.</i>

77
00:05:35,794 --> 00:05:39,006
<i>He loses, they take him away.</i>
<i>Another mother left sobbing.</i>

78
00:05:39,089 --> 00:05:41,467
<i>He'll be sent to Hell's Coast.</i>

79
00:05:41,550 --> 00:05:44,636
<i>Sold into slavery,</i>
<i>his soul lost to the devil.</i>

80
00:05:46,138 --> 00:05:49,516
Animal! Animal in the Perimeter!

81
00:05:52,811 --> 00:05:55,439
<i>Run, Rooster! This is too risky.</i>

82
00:05:55,522 --> 00:05:57,357
Turn left down that alley.

83
00:06:00,110 --> 00:06:02,154
He's there!

84
00:06:03,906 --> 00:06:05,532
Rooster! Look, he's there!

85
00:06:06,617 --> 00:06:08,619
Shit, he's in. Go!

86
00:06:19,129 --> 00:06:20,547
The Hunter has seen you.

87
00:06:21,298 --> 00:06:23,300
Go down the alleyway. Run!

88
00:06:23,383 --> 00:06:24,802
<i>No one gets past the Hunter.</i>

89
00:06:24,885 --> 00:06:26,637
<i>That Rooster is screwed!</i>

90
00:06:27,805 --> 00:06:28,889
Take down that drone.

91
00:06:30,432 --> 00:06:31,892
NO SIGNAL

92
00:06:33,352 --> 00:06:34,603
Well, that's it.

93
00:07:09,596 --> 00:07:11,640
<i>The animals are on the homestretch.</i>

94
00:07:11,723 --> 00:07:15,394
<i>The first two win a fortune</i>
<i>and save their collateral.</i>

95
00:07:21,400 --> 00:07:25,821
<i>Bull, Horse, Tigress and Goat running</i>
<i>for a life-changing prize.</i>

96
00:07:28,949 --> 00:07:32,744
<i>Inside the Complex, Bull seems to already</i>
<i>know he will be a three-time champion.</i>

97
00:07:34,830 --> 00:07:38,000
<i>Release the heifers, guys!</i>
<i>This one is Bull's.</i>

98
00:07:39,001 --> 00:07:41,253
Come on! Go!

99
00:07:41,336 --> 00:07:43,172
Go, Bull!

100
00:07:47,843 --> 00:07:52,514
{\an8}1ST BULL - TIME 48:11:68
2 WINS - 2 LOSSES

101
00:07:52,598 --> 00:07:56,768
BEAST RACE

102
00:08:00,355 --> 00:08:02,900
Are you crazy? That's fucking cowardice!

103
00:08:02,983 --> 00:08:05,444
Fuck! Damn.

104
00:08:07,696 --> 00:08:09,448
It's over, brother. It's over.

105
00:08:10,282 --> 00:08:12,201
I've got two kids. Think of them.

106
00:08:12,784 --> 00:08:15,078
You should have thought of that before.

107
00:08:16,330 --> 00:08:18,123
Are you the one feeding them?

108
00:08:20,417 --> 00:08:22,336
And your collateral,
isn't he worth something?

109
00:08:25,255 --> 00:08:28,300
Bring him, but no messing around!

110
00:08:35,891 --> 00:08:37,059
You won.

111
00:08:40,938 --> 00:08:41,772
Let's go.

112
00:08:44,942 --> 00:08:47,027
Those who bet on Rooster lost,

113
00:08:47,110 --> 00:08:50,239
but the real loser was his collateral.

114
00:08:50,322 --> 00:08:53,909
<i>Too many innocent people have been lost.</i>
<i>Enslaved on Hell's Coast.</i>

115
00:08:53,992 --> 00:08:56,787
<i>Guinea pigs in genetic labs.</i>

116
00:08:56,870 --> 00:08:58,956
<i>The Perimeter will take the game down.</i>

117
00:08:59,039 --> 00:09:01,833
<i>And you are all</i>
<i>going to come down with it.</i>

118
00:09:02,501 --> 00:09:05,837
<i>That's all, folks!</i>
<i>It's the end of the season.</i>

119
00:09:05,921 --> 00:09:08,632
<i>From the 20 that began</i>
<i>to the five finalists,</i>

120
00:09:08,715 --> 00:09:12,636
<i>we saw them fighting it out</i>
<i>on that jungle of a track over four heats.</i>

121
00:09:14,471 --> 00:09:16,765
<i>And Bull wins yet another season.</i>

122
00:09:16,848 --> 00:09:21,311
<i>He won two of four heats and took it all.</i>

123
00:09:22,562 --> 00:09:24,147
Nice, man. Another one.

124
00:09:26,316 --> 00:09:27,776
Let me get your collateral.

125
00:09:28,568 --> 00:09:30,237
They are here.

126
00:09:37,577 --> 00:09:39,454
You guys are mistreated.

127
00:09:40,539 --> 00:09:42,499
What kind of a fucking car is that?

128
00:09:45,002 --> 00:09:46,336
Say hi to your family.

129
00:09:54,219 --> 00:09:55,762
{\an8}1ST BULL 2ND HORSE

130
00:09:56,680 --> 00:09:59,391
<i>Bull's a three-time champion.</i>
<i>Only Rooster didn't make it.</i>

131
00:09:59,474 --> 00:10:01,351
<i>But that's the game.</i>

132
00:10:01,435 --> 00:10:03,478
I'm Divina, beasties.

133
00:10:03,562 --> 00:10:05,439
The voice of the show for those who bet.

134
00:10:05,522 --> 00:10:08,817
<i>It's illegal, it's cruel,</i>
<i>but that's what people want.</i>

135
00:10:08,900 --> 00:10:10,986
Next season, I'll be on the track.

136
00:10:11,987 --> 00:10:14,823
And things will be better. Okay?

137
00:10:16,950 --> 00:10:18,535
Bet wrong again, Dad?

138
00:10:20,078 --> 00:10:21,079
Yeah.

139
00:10:21,663 --> 00:10:24,583
Soon you will all be betting on me.

140
00:10:24,666 --> 00:10:26,460
Take note. Don't forget.

141
00:10:29,087 --> 00:10:32,591
Hey! Bring the car
to take this animal to the health clinic.

142
00:10:35,385 --> 00:10:36,428
Another one, huh?

143
00:10:43,310 --> 00:10:44,394
Congrats.

144
00:10:45,103 --> 00:10:46,980
You are quite the celebrity, man.

145
00:10:55,030 --> 00:10:56,073
And the chicken?

146
00:10:56,907 --> 00:10:58,033
Who's his collateral?

147
00:10:58,867 --> 00:10:59,868
His nephew.

148
00:11:01,078 --> 00:11:04,539
-Let him go! Come on!
-Mom!

149
00:11:04,623 --> 00:11:07,959
The kid's barely 18,
and he's in the hands of that gang.

150
00:11:10,212 --> 00:11:11,505
No!

151
00:11:13,965 --> 00:11:17,052
And you guys want to do what?
Take him to the health clinic?

152
00:11:17,135 --> 00:11:18,887
Since when is that your problem?

153
00:11:26,228 --> 00:11:27,270
Take your shirt off.

154
00:11:29,314 --> 00:11:30,565
Go on, take it off.

155
00:11:32,692 --> 00:11:33,777
Come on.

156
00:11:36,905 --> 00:11:41,827
We've got an opportunity
and only you two can't see it.

157
00:11:41,910 --> 00:11:44,413
Even more so
with the skin market on the rise.

158
00:11:45,247 --> 00:11:47,165
This right here is worth a bomb.

159
00:11:47,874 --> 00:11:51,795
An animal like this, with a track record.
Look at this, worth a fortune.

160
00:11:52,671 --> 00:11:56,550
-Money for the Perimeter's security.
-Selling human skin.

161
00:11:57,175 --> 00:11:58,343
You are sick, Sinatra.

162
00:11:59,761 --> 00:12:02,514
Don't you have any idea
how shit goes down here?

163
00:12:03,265 --> 00:12:06,810
If you still don't get it, get lost.
Go jump in a lake.

164
00:12:06,893 --> 00:12:09,479
-Little flower, we want the same thing.
-Yeah?

165
00:12:09,563 --> 00:12:11,064
We just disagree on the method.

166
00:12:12,691 --> 00:12:14,693
And don't forget I was born here,
you pacifist.

167
00:12:15,944 --> 00:12:18,655
I'm not a dirty little creature
raised by an animal.

168
00:12:30,876 --> 00:12:32,169
Get moving.

169
00:12:33,003 --> 00:12:35,380
The circus is over. Get moving.

170
00:12:50,187 --> 00:12:53,064
-What's up, Dalva?
-They suspended me.

171
00:12:53,690 --> 00:12:55,817
That bastard, son of a bitch.

172
00:12:56,693 --> 00:12:59,529
I'm going to end up losing
this fucking job, Mano.

173
00:13:01,823 --> 00:13:03,450
I can't take it anymore, really.

174
00:13:05,452 --> 00:13:06,870
<i>We are going to find a way.</i>

175
00:13:08,955 --> 00:13:11,625
-How's Baco?
-The same.

176
00:13:12,626 --> 00:13:13,710
Actually, he's worse.

177
00:13:13,793 --> 00:13:16,963
Drinking more,
spending money we don't have.

178
00:13:18,298 --> 00:13:21,426
-Betting?
-Yes.

179
00:13:27,641 --> 00:13:31,520
-Come on.
-Why do you like this sewer?

180
00:13:31,603 --> 00:13:33,104
Best to stick to the shade.

181
00:13:33,730 --> 00:13:36,358
As an animal hunter,
I'm not exactly Rio's favorite guy.

182
00:13:38,193 --> 00:13:40,195
I wish I had lived back then.

183
00:13:40,278 --> 00:13:41,655
It's pretty.

184
00:13:43,198 --> 00:13:45,825
But they all died
in the Great Catastrophe.

185
00:13:45,909 --> 00:13:48,203
We are lucky to be here.

186
00:13:49,371 --> 00:13:52,457
Lucky? Living with all this crap?

187
00:13:55,669 --> 00:13:56,586
What is it?

188
00:13:58,088 --> 00:13:59,506
The star of the final.

189
00:14:03,635 --> 00:14:04,719
I want an autograph.

190
00:14:07,055 --> 00:14:08,223
Dalva.

191
00:14:09,224 --> 00:14:10,183
You've grown.

192
00:14:12,769 --> 00:14:15,522
The high point of the race
was when you took Rooster out.

193
00:14:15,605 --> 00:14:16,773
Always here to help.

194
00:14:17,440 --> 00:14:18,733
I should be mad, right?

195
00:14:20,610 --> 00:14:23,238
Every day I get a whole bunch of kids
wanting to run.

196
00:14:24,281 --> 00:14:28,159
But a good animal, who can last
7-8 kilometers out there, is hard to find.

197
00:14:29,703 --> 00:14:32,914
Rooster was one,
and he's not the first you've taken out.

198
00:14:33,582 --> 00:14:35,083
And he won't be the last.

199
00:14:36,042 --> 00:14:37,294
What's your plan?

200
00:14:38,920 --> 00:14:42,215
You were always promising.
You could be out there winning.

201
00:14:43,174 --> 00:14:45,468
Run for me,
rather than away from me, damn it.

202
00:14:47,596 --> 00:14:48,722
I'll pay you double.

203
00:14:56,938 --> 00:14:58,189
I'll do it.

204
00:14:59,316 --> 00:15:03,153
The day no animal has to lose someone
as collateral like I did.

205
00:15:04,404 --> 00:15:06,990
Life's no fun without the drama.

206
00:15:07,073 --> 00:15:08,366
I don't give a fuck.

207
00:15:14,581 --> 00:15:17,459
If you want to keep playing
at getting in our way,

208
00:15:18,335 --> 00:15:20,962
rather than getting her
or your stepfather out of poverty,

209
00:15:21,046 --> 00:15:22,047
that's up to you.

210
00:15:27,510 --> 00:15:30,388
But remember I can bring your life
as the Hunter to an end.

211
00:15:32,098 --> 00:15:33,224
Whenever I want.

212
00:15:55,497 --> 00:15:57,957
-The landlord came.
-What did he want, Dad?

213
00:15:58,458 --> 00:16:02,045
-He wants 8000 a week.
-He's going to keep raising it.

214
00:16:02,671 --> 00:16:06,132
Why don't you move to the Perimeter?
You don't get this there.

215
00:16:06,216 --> 00:16:10,178
And live with a bunch of crazy people
who believe they will end the game?

216
00:16:10,970 --> 00:16:12,681
I raised you two by running.

217
00:16:12,764 --> 00:16:13,973
And you lost our mom.

218
00:16:14,057 --> 00:16:17,185
Look here, boy, don't talk
about what you don't understand.

219
00:16:17,977 --> 00:16:20,313
Don't talk about
what you don't understand.

220
00:16:21,231 --> 00:16:25,527
What do you think is going to happen
when I walk into the fucking Perimeter?

221
00:16:26,069 --> 00:16:29,155
Do you think I want to be judged
for running as an animal?

222
00:16:32,075 --> 00:16:33,702
I know how they will look at me.

223
00:16:35,912 --> 00:16:38,957
Exactly. Just the way you are right now.

224
00:16:47,465 --> 00:16:48,675
Ungrateful.

225
00:16:57,392 --> 00:16:59,102
He lived here with Mom.

226
00:16:59,602 --> 00:17:01,563
He will leave only when he's dead.

227
00:17:02,772 --> 00:17:04,899
It seems like that's what he wants.

228
00:17:04,983 --> 00:17:07,193
Fuck, Mano, you should be running.

229
00:17:07,902 --> 00:17:11,865
Helping your family, but no,
you are against the game.

230
00:17:13,241 --> 00:17:15,577
And he's offering you double to play.

231
00:17:16,286 --> 00:17:18,288
How can you think that?

232
00:17:19,748 --> 00:17:24,836
There is a guy in this house
